      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a good start, but I'm worried. I was looking over that leaked impact report again—the one showing how Section 4 actually creates a massive cost burden for the smaller manufacturers in his district. If Miller finds out that \"de-risking investment\" actually means squeezing out the local guys, he's going to bury us.\n\nHow do we handle that specific point if he brings up the cost burden/impact on small manufacturers? I need to know we've got a way to spin that, or at least a way to make it seem like a minor, manageable transition period rather than a deal-breaker.",
